  "query_preview": "..(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 425 AM EDT FRI AUG 28 2026\n\nThe most current model data sticks with the idea of broad 5h\nridging covering much of the southeast quadrant of the country\nthrough the weekend and well into the new work week. Any model \ndifferences seem to be confined to the northern international\nborder region - too far away to have an impact on the weather for\neastern Kentucky. Some weakness in the large ridge with time \ncould allow for convection to return to the forecast by mid-week -\nmainly in the higher southeastern terrain initially then possibly\na chance for the entire area on Thursday. Regardless, the end of\nthe month and start of September will be primarily remembered for\nits warmth and mainly dry conditions.",
